# Civil War Strategy: the special events that favor the South, each forced by the dice
# (tests/README.md, "Forced dice"). The game is loaded from a prepared save: November 1863, the
# Rebels hold 30 cities. The Union only ends each turn, and the computer is passive.
#   November 1863   riots in Tullahoma, a city the Union took
#   January 1864    50 victory points for the South; England gives it ships
#   March 1864      British mercenaries join an army
#   May 1864        no event
#   July 1864       a fifth of the Union's forces take furloughs to vote
#   September, November 1864   no event
#   January 1865    100 victory points for the South; a loan from Europe
# A digest at each main menu, and the history file, which names each event.
#! seed 1863
#! cfg history=1 bold=0
#! data events-south
#! dice 0,.05,.95,.91;0,.05,.5,0;0,.05,.5,.9,0,.9;1;0,.05,.5,.9,.9,.9,.9,.1;1;1;0,.05,.5,.9,.9,.1
#! files cws.his

# Pauses that any key ends; End Turn and End Game: Yes; a Retreat: the first city; the
# Options at the game's end: Quit this Game.
rule 1 key space
rule 2:E text y
rule 2:R key enter
rule 2:O text q

# The title menu: Resume Saved Game; the Load menu: the one save.
play until 2:V
text r
play until 2:L
key enter

# The main menu: UTILITY, End Cond. Victory Conditions starts on Time: down and Enter turn
# off each of the four others. Esc there, and Esc at the Utility menu.
play until 2:M
digest
text u
prompt
text e
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key esc
prompt
key esc

# Each month's main menu: a digest, then END TURN.
repeat 8
play until 2:M
digest
text e
end

# March 1865: the time is up and the game ends. The Hall of Fame asks for the commander's name.
play until 4
text Tester
key enter
play until 1:G
digest
key space

# The title menu: Quit to DOS, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
play until 2:V
digest
text q
repeat space
